'''Unarmed combat''',<ref name="Master & Apprentice">''[[Master & Apprentice]]''</ref> '''hand-to-hand combat''',<ref name="Complete Vehicles 2018">[[Star Wars: Complete Vehicles (2018)|''Star Wars: Complete Vehicles'' (2018)]]</ref> or '''martial arts''',<ref name="Bazine Netal">{{SWCT|set=2020 Base Series 2|cardname=Bazine Netal}}</ref> was a variety of combat in which no distance weapons were used, as opposed to firefights.<ref name="Master & Apprentice" /> A person who practiced martial arts was known as [[martial artist]].<ref name="ND">[[No Disintegrations (Fantasy Flight Games)|''No Disintegrations'']]</ref>

==History==
While their rival [[Planet|world]] of [[E'ronoh]] had required military training for all citizens, [[Prince]] [[Phan-tu Zenn]] of [[Eiram]] claimed his world did not have hand-to-hand combat.<ref name="Convergence">''[[The High Republic: Convergence]]''</ref> The [[Zygerrian]]s had a tradition of resolving their differences by unarmed combat.<ref name="Kidnapped">{{TCW|Kidnapped}}</ref> Known fighting moves included the [[Strike of the Nexu]] and the [[Kick of the Bantha]].<ref name="DD">''[[Dark Disciple]]''</ref> The [[bounty hunter]] [[Latts Razzi]] was an expert in several forms of exotic martial arts. The [[Battle droid|combat droid]] [[C-21 Highsinger]] studied Razzi's martial arts moves in order to imitate her deadly fighting style.<ref name="SWE C-21 Highsinger">{{SWE|characters|c21highsinger|C-21 Highsinger}}</ref>

[[Mitth'raw'nuruodo]] was skilled at unarmed combat and was familiar with the limitations of the [[Imperial Academy]] martial art. The [[Grand Admiral]] managed to defeat [[Alexsandr Kallus|Kallus]] in hand to hand combat. Kallus was also skilled in hand to hand combat; having managed to hold the [[Chiss]] at bay for a while until he was kicked in the head. The force of the kick sent him flying into a barrier, resulting in the fight ending.<ref name="Zero Hour">{{Rebels|Zero Hour}}</ref>

